1b:T400,In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:

af_unix: Set gc_in_progress to true in unix_gc().

Igor Ushakov reported that unix_gc() could run with gc_in_progress
being false if the work is scheduled while running:

  Thread 1         Thread 2                     Thread 3
  --------         --------                     --------
                   unix_schedule_gc()           unix_schedule_gc()
                   `- if (!gc_in_progress)      `- if (!gc_in_progress)
                      |- gc_in_progress = true     |
                      `- queue_work()              |
  unix_gc() <----------------/                     |
  |                                                |- gc_in_progress = true
  ...                                              `- queue_work()
  |                                                       |
  `- gc_in_progress = false                               |
                                                          |
  unix_gc() <------------------------------------10:["$","main",null,{"children":["$","$L1a",null,{"initialData":[{"id":"1331359699","cve_id":"CVE-2026-23745","name":"node-tar-cve-demo","owner":"OndrejDrapalik","full_name":"OndrejDrapalik/node-tar-cve-demo","html_url":"https://github.com/OndrejDrapalik/node-tar-cve-demo","description":"Mirror of isaacs/node-tar pinned at 8bb83f7 — the commit before the CVE-2026-23745 fix. Demo target for autonomous vulnerability patching. Do not install from here; use node-tar 7.5.3+.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"node-tar is a Tar for Node.js. The node-tar library (<= 7.5.2) fails to sanitize the linkpath of Link (hardlink) and SymbolicLink entries when preservePaths is false (the default secure behavior). This allows malicious archives to bypass the extraction root restriction, leading to Arbitrary File Overwrite via hardlinks and Symlink Poisoning via absolute symlink targets. This vulnerability is fixed in 7.5.3.","created_at":"2026-08-12 06:16:44","updated_at":"2026-08-12 06:20:28","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 06:20:18","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.2,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1331343761","cve_id":"CVE-2024-21413","name":"tryhackme-moniker-link","owner":"yfelipecruvinel","full_name":"yfelipecruvinel/tryhackme-moniker-link","html_url":"https://github.com/yfelipecruvinel/tryhackme-moniker-link","description":"Documentation of my  hands-on lab Moniker Link (CVE-2024-21413) completed on TryHackMe.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Microsoft Outlook Remote Code Execution Vulnerability","created_at":"2026-08-12 05:51:44","updated_at":"2026-08-12 06:20:06","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 06:19:19","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:07","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1331337390","cve_id":"CVE-2025-64459","name":"CVE-2025-64459","owner":"YouGina","full_name":"YouGina/CVE-2025-64459","html_url":"https://github.com/YouGina/CVE-2025-64459","description":"CVE-2025-64459 vulnerable by design app","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An issue was discovered in 5.1 before 5.1.14, 4.2 before 4.2.26, and 5.2 before 5.2.8.\nThe methods `QuerySet.filter()`, `QuerySet.exclude()`, and `QuerySet.get()`, and the class `Q()`, are subject to SQL injection when using a suitably crafted dictionary, with dictionary expansion, as the `_connector` argument.\nEarlier, unsupported Django series (such as 5.0.x, 4.1.x, and 3.2.x) were not evaluated and may also be affected.\nDjango would like to thank cyberstan for reporting this issue.","created_at":"2026-08-12 05:42:10","updated_at":"2026-08-12 05:44:15","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 05:43:59","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:09","cvss_score":9.1,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1331304720","cve_id":"CVE-2025-5781","name":"CVE-2025-5781","owner":"jasonbernier","full_name":"jasonbernier/CVE-2025-5781","html_url":"https://github.com/jasonbernier/CVE-2025-5781","description":"CVE-2025-5781 FreePBX Exploit POC","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Information Exposure Vulnerability in Hitachi Ops Center API Configuration Manager, Hitachi Configuration Manager, Hitachi Device Manager allows Session Hijacking.This issue affects Hitachi Ops Center API Configuration Manager: from 10.0.0-00 before 11.0.5-00; Hitachi Configuration Manager: from 8.5.1-00 before 11.0.5-00; Hitachi Device Manager: from 8.4.1-00 before 8.6.5-00.","created_at":"2026-08-12 04:55:00","updated_at":"2026-08-12 05:02:39","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 05:02:25","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:08","cvss_score":5.2,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1331262219","cve_id":"CVE-2026-45585","name":"YellowKey-Bitlocker-CVE-2026-45585","owner":"yellowkeycve","full_name":"yellowkeycve/YellowKey-Bitlocker-CVE-2026-45585","html_url":"https://github.com/yellowkeycve/YellowKey-Bitlocker-CVE-2026-45585","description":"YellowKey BitLocker CVE-2026-45585 - free BitLocker recovery key extractor and vulnerability tool. Bitlocker yellowkey, yellowkey bitlocker, yellowkey github, cve-2026-45585, yellowkey vulnerability, yellowkey exploit, chaotic eclipse. Free 2026.","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"Microsoft is aware of a security feature bypass vulnerability in Windows publicly referred to as &quot;YellowKey&quot;. The proof of concept for this vulnerability has been made public violating coordinated vulnerability best practices.\nWe are issuing this CVE to provide mitigation guidance that can be implemented to protect against this vulnerability until the security update is made available.","created_at":"2026-08-12 03:59:40","updated_at":"2026-08-12 04:18:43","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 04:18:39","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:09","cvss_score":6.8,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1331252029","cve_id":"CVE-2026-62737","name":"CVE-2026-62737-POC","owner":"0p5cur","full_name":"0p5cur/CVE-2026-62737-POC","html_url":"https://github.com/0p5cur/CVE-2026-62737-POC","description":"CVE-2026-24061's poc","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-12 03:47:22","updated_at":"2026-08-12 03:51:16","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 03:51:11","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 04:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1331161172","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64564","name":"yc-mk8s-sctphantom-mitigation","owner":"yandex-cloud-examples","full_name":"yandex-cloud-examples/yc-mk8s-sctphantom-mitigation","html_url":"https://github.com/yandex-cloud-examples/yc-mk8s-sctphantom-mitigation","description":"DaemonSet для митигации уязвимости CVE-2026-64564 (SCTPhantom)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-12 02:01:12","updated_at":"2026-08-12 02:28:44","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 02:27:40","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 04:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1331031130","cve_id":"CVE-2022-35914","name":"CVE-2022-35914-RCE","owner":"cyb3rk0ala","full_name":"cyb3rk0ala/CVE-2022-35914-RCE","html_url":"https://github.com/cyb3rk0ala/CVE-2022-35914-RCE","description":"PoC exploit for CVE-2022-35914 — GLPI htmLawed command injection, command execution, and reverse shell support.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"/vendor/htmlawed/htmlawed/htmLawedTest.php in the htmlawed module for GLPI through 10.0.2 allows PHP code injection.","created_at":"2026-08-11 23:42:31","updated_at":"2026-08-12 00:48:33","pushed_at":"2026-08-12 00:47:36","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 04:37:07","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1330847222","cve_id":"CVE-2026-17106","name":"CVE-2026-17106","owner":"HackSpeak","full_name":"HackSpeak/CVE-2026-17106","html_url":"https://github.com/HackSpeak/CVE-2026-17106","description":"CopyEscape (CVE-2026-17106) docker cp container-to-host arbitrary file write PoC mirror — Imperva Ron Masas, MIT; for authorized security testing","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11 20:34:39","updated_at":"2026-08-11 20:35:35","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 20:35:07","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 22:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1330685294","cve_id":"CVE-2026-44401","name":"CVE-2026-44401","owner":"sn0x-sharma","full_name":"sn0x-sharma/CVE-2026-44401","html_url":"https://github.com/sn0x-sharma/CVE-2026-44401","description":"Persistent XSS in Typemill CMS: the Markdown parser lets javascript: URIs through unfiltered. Writeup + PoC.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11 17:38:58","updated_at":"2026-08-11 18:13:58","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 17:56:49","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 22:37:09","cvss_score":4.6,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1330669803","cve_id":"CVE-2026-48710","name":"CVE-2026-48710","owner":"CuteeCat","full_name":"CuteeCat/CVE-2026-48710","html_url":"https://github.com/CuteeCat/CVE-2026-48710","description":"CVE-2026-48710漏洞验证代码","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Starlette is a lightweight ASGI framework/toolkit. Prior to version 1.0.1, the HTTP `Host` request header was not validated before being used to reconstruct `request.url`. Because the routing algorithm relies on the raw HTTP path while `request.url` is rebuilt from the `Host` header, a malformed header could make `request.url.path` differ from the path that was actually requested. Middleware and endpoints that apply security restrictions based on `request.url` (rather than the raw `scope` path) could therefore be bypassed. Users should upgrade to a version greater than or equal to version 1.0.1, which validates the `Host` header against the grammar of RFC 9112 §3.2 / RFC 3986 §3.2.2 when constructing `request.url` and falls back to `scope[\"server\"]` for malformed values.","created_at":"2026-08-11 17:21:36","updated_at":"2026-08-11 17:42:36","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 17:42:30","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 22:37:09","cvss_score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1330601329","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"ghostlock-cve-2026-43499-4.19-k40","owner":"yijiacloud","full_name":"yijiacloud/ghostlock-cve-2026-43499-4.19-k40","html_url":"https://github.com/yijiacloud/ghostlock-cve-2026-43499-4.19-k40","description":"CVE-2026-43499 (GhostLock) rtmutex remove_waiter() UAF local-root PoC adapted for Qualcomm Android 4.19 kernels (Redmi K40 / Snapdragon 870 class), LD_PRELOAD based","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 16:00:12","updated_at":"2026-08-11 21:29:32","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 21:29:25","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 22:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330594791","cve_id":"CVE-2026-18830","name":"aegisagent","owner":"huzjie","full_name":"huzjie/aegisagent","html_url":"https://github.com/huzjie/aegisagent","description":"AegisAgent - Runtime security gateway & privilege governance for AI agents. Cryptographic tool-call provenance (CoreBreak/CVE-2026-18830/18236/64650 defense), policy engine, sandbox isolation, HITL approval, MCP security proxy, tamper-evident audit.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11 15:52:24","updated_at":"2026-08-11 15:52:25","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 15:52:25","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":8.1,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330585167","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"GhostLock-OPPO-PCKM00","owner":"yijiacloud","full_name":"yijiacloud/GhostLock-OPPO-PCKM00","html_url":"https://github.com/yijiacloud/GhostLock-OPPO-PCKM00","description":"CVE-2026-43499 GhostLock futex UAF LPE PoC for OPPO PCKM00 (SM6150) / Linux 4.14.180","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 15:40:53","updated_at":"2026-08-11 15:41:09","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 15:41:05","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330488045","cve_id":"CVE-2026-18577","name":"stormencryptor-ncentral-defense","owner":"Yash-Dalvee","full_name":"Yash-Dalvee/stormencryptor-ncentral-defense","html_url":"https://github.com/Yash-Dalvee/stormencryptor-ncentral-defense","description":"Defensive security research, SIEM rules, and remediation tools for CVE-2026-18577 & StormEncryptor ransomware.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11 13:22:52","updated_at":"2026-08-11 13:22:53","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 13:22:52","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":8.2,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330424371","cve_id":"CVE-2025-69286","name":"ragflow-audit","owner":"qianlijaingshan","full_name":"qianlijaingshan/ragflow-audit","html_url":"https://github.com/qianlijaingshan/ragflow-audit","description":"RAGFlow 三洞审计工具 (CVE-2026-28797 / CVE-2026-24770 / CVE-2025-69286)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"RAGFlow is an open-source RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) engine. In versions prior to 0.22.0, the use of an insecure key generation algorithm in the API key and beta (assistant/agent share auth) token generation process allows these tokens to be mutually derivable. Specifically, both tokens are generated using the same `URLSafeTimedSerializer` with predictable inputs, enabling an unauthorized user who obtains the shared assistant/agent URL to derive the personal API key. This grants them full control over the assistant/agent owner's account. Version 0.22.0 fixes the issue.","created_at":"2026-08-11 11:36:51","updated_at":"2026-08-11 11:44:57","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 11:44:54","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:08","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330423837","cve_id":"CVE-2026-2766","name":"CVE-2026-2766-but-with-wasm","owner":"SneakyNachos","full_name":"SneakyNachos/CVE-2026-2766-but-with-wasm","html_url":"https://github.com/SneakyNachos/CVE-2026-2766-but-with-wasm","description":"CVE-2026-2766, but with wasm","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Use-after-free in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component. This vulnerability was fixed in Firefox 148, Firefox ESR 140.8, Thunderbird 148, and Thunderbird 140.8.","created_at":"2026-08-11 11:36:01","updated_at":"2026-08-11 11:36:08","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 11:36:04","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1330379607","cve_id":"CVE-2026-2764","name":"CVE-2026-2764-but-with-wasm","owner":"SneakyNachos","full_name":"SneakyNachos/CVE-2026-2764-but-with-wasm","html_url":"https://github.com/SneakyNachos/CVE-2026-2764-but-with-wasm","description":"CVE-2026-2764, but with wasm","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"JIT miscompilation, use-after-free in the JavaScript Engine: JIT component. This vulnerability was fixed in Firefox 148, Firefox ESR 115.33, Firefox ESR 140.8, Thunderbird 148, and Thunderbird 140.8.","created_at":"2026-08-11 10:19:14","updated_at":"2026-08-11 10:19:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 10:19:17","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1330367031","cve_id":"CVE-2026-9198","name":"CVE-2026-9198","owner":"CuteeCat","full_name":"CuteeCat/CVE-2026-9198","html_url":"https://github.com/CuteeCat/CVE-2026-9198","description":"CVE-2026-9198利用代码","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-11 09:55:44","updated_at":"2026-08-11 10:05:17","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 10:05:11","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1330335788","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"ghostlock-skeleton-v2","owner":"oopnv70-lab","full_name":"oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-skeleton-v2","html_url":"https://github.com/oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-skeleton-v2","description":"CVE-2026-43499 GhostLock APK 骨架 — 从零开始，仅空项目编译验证","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 08:53:29","updated_at":"2026-08-11 09:10:54","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 09:10:50","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330335520","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"ghostlock-skeleton","owner":"oopnv70-lab","full_name":"oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-skeleton","html_url":"https://github.com/oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-skeleton","description":"CVE-2026-43499 GhostLock APK 骨架 — 仅验证空项目能编译通过","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 08:53:00","updated_at":"2026-08-11 08:53:01","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 08:53:01","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330331440","cve_id":"CVE-2020-25279","name":"Firmware-analysis","owner":"Gimminse","full_name":"Gimminse/Firmware-analysis","html_url":"https://github.com/Gimminse/Firmware-analysis","description":"Rediscovered CVE-2020-25279, a critical vulnerability in the Shannon baseband used in Samsung Exynos chipsets","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An issue was discovered on Samsung mobile devices with O(8.x), P(9.0), and Q(10.0) (Exynos chipsets) software. The baseband component has a buffer overflow via an abnormal SETUP message, leading to execution of arbitrary code. The Samsung ID is SVE-2020-18098 (September 2020).","created_at":"2026-08-11 08:44:30","updated_at":"2026-08-11 08:47:00","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 08:46:55","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:06","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1330322995","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"ghostlock-x200-root","owner":"xiaohj233","full_name":"xiaohj233/ghostlock-x200-root","html_url":"https://github.com/xiaohj233/ghostlock-x200-root","description":"GhostLock-X200 v1.0 - temporary root toolchain for vivo X200 (PD2415 / b57 kernel) based on CVE-2026-43499. For authorized security research only.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 08:26:52","updated_at":"2026-08-11 08:31:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 08:30:41","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330317650","cve_id":"CVE-2025-7771","name":"CVE-2025-7771","owner":"enessakircolak","full_name":"enessakircolak/CVE-2025-7771","html_url":"https://github.com/enessakircolak/CVE-2025-7771","description":"ThrottleStop.sys Arbitrary Physical Memory R/W","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"ThrottleStop.sys, a legitimate driver, exposes two IOCTL interfaces that allow arbitrary read and write access to physical memory via the MmMapIoSpace function. This insecure implementation can be exploited by a malicious user-mode application to patch the running Windows kernel and invoke arbitrary kernel functions with ring-0 privileges. The vulnerability enables local attackers to execute arbitrary code in kernel context, resulting in privilege escalation and potential follow-on attacks, such as disabling security software or bypassing kernel-level protections. ThrottleStop.sys version 3.0.0.0 and possibly others are affected. Apply updates per vendor instructions.","created_at":"2026-08-11 08:15:36","updated_at":"2026-08-11 08:46:13","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 08:15:39","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.7,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330278156","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"ghostlock-apk","owner":"oopnv70-lab","full_name":"oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-apk","html_url":"https://github.com/oopnv70-lab/ghostlock-apk","description":"独立 APK：CVE-2026-43499 GhostLock 提权 + Shizuku shell 身份执行","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-11 07:00:35","updated_at":"2026-08-11 07:54:55","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 07:54:49","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330207727","cve_id":"CVE-2025-2945","name":"CVE-2025-2945","owner":"g0d150ne","full_name":"g0d150ne/CVE-2025-2945","html_url":"https://github.com/g0d150ne/CVE-2025-2945","description":"Exploit for pgAdmin4 Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability affecting versions 8.10 to 9.1.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Remote Code Execution security vulnerability in pgAdmin 4  (Query Tool and Cloud Deployment modules).\n\nThe vulnerability is associated with the 2 POST endpoints; /sqleditor/query_tool/download, where the query_commited parameter and /cloud/deploy endpoint, where the high_availability parameter is unsafely passed to the Python eval() function, allowing arbitrary code execution.\n\n\nThis issue affects pgAdmin 4: before 9.2.","created_at":"2026-08-11 05:06:45","updated_at":"2026-08-11 05:52:45","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 05:52:33","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":9.9,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1330202833","cve_id":"CVE-2026-53361","name":"bad_garbage","owner":"sgkdev","full_name":"sgkdev/bad_garbage","html_url":"https://github.com/sgkdev/bad_garbage","description":"CVE-2026-53361 AF_UNIX GC vs MSG_PEEK use-after-free container escape","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"$1b","created_at":"2026-08-11 04:59:45","updated_at":"2026-08-12 06:26:00","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 20:43:30","inserted_at":"2026-08-12 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.1,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1330145106","cve_id":"CVE-2021-47881","name":"CVE-2021-47881","owner":"kagancapar","full_name":"kagancapar/CVE-2021-47881","html_url":"https://github.com/kagancapar/CVE-2021-47881","description":"CVE-2021-47881: Local stack buffer overflow in dataSIMS Avionics ARINC 664-1 v4.5.3 (CWE-121)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"dataSIMS Avionics ARINC 664-1 version 4.5.3 contains a local buffer overflow vulnerability that allows attackers to overwrite memory by manipulating the milstd1553result.txt file. Attackers can craft a malicious file with carefully constructed payload and alignment sections to potentially execute arbitrary code on the Windows system.","created_at":"2026-08-11 03:43:45","updated_at":"2026-08-11 03:47:04","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 03:44:44","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:07","cvss_score":6.7,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329978743","cve_id":"CVE-2025-71329","name":"image-size-next","owner":"lcf2212dev","full_name":"lcf2212dev/image-size-next","html_url":"https://github.com/lcf2212dev/image-size-next","description":"Community-maintained fork of image-size with fixes for CVE-2025-71329 and CVE-2025-71330","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"image-size through 2.0.2 contains a denial of service vulnerability that allows remote attackers to permanently block the Node.js event loop by supplying a specially crafted image buffer with a zero-valued size field in a recognized box-type. Attackers can trigger an infinite loop in the JXL or HEIF image parsers by providing a crafted image containing a box with a size of zero, causing the offset to never advance and permanently hanging the application.","created_at":"2026-08-11 00:36:09","updated_at":"2026-08-11 02:03:04","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 02:01:56","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 04:37:08","cvss_score":8.7,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329933363","cve_id":"CVE-2026-34348","name":"CVE-2026-34348","owner":"HORKimhab","full_name":"HORKimhab/CVE-2026-34348","html_url":"https://github.com/HORKimhab/CVE-2026-34348","description":"CVE-2026-34348 - Draft or TODO","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 23:48:40","updated_at":"2026-08-10 23:52:49","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 23:52:27","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 04:37:08","cvss_score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329908938","cve_id":"CVE-2026-65891","name":"CVE-2026-65891","owner":"murrez","full_name":"murrez/CVE-2026-65891","html_url":"https://github.com/murrez/CVE-2026-65891","description":"CVE-2026-65891 PoC — Joomla Content Editor file rename vulnerability (auth required, fixed in JCE 2.20.2)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 23:22:57","updated_at":"2026-08-10 23:26:20","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 23:23:33","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 04:37:08","cvss_score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329796215","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64824","name":"CVE-2026-64824-PoC","owner":"Boreas37","full_name":"Boreas37/CVE-2026-64824-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/Boreas37/CVE-2026-64824-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-64824 — Home Assistant backup-restore symlink path traversal → root RCE. First working PoC, verified on real HA 2026.5.4 (sitecustomize.py overwrite). GHSA-cwh8-w64c-4j5h","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 21:21:47","updated_at":"2026-08-10 21:22:26","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 21:21:51","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:10","cvss_score":9.3,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329768131","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64747","name":"agxprobe","owner":"jiuyi155","full_name":"jiuyi155/agxprobe","html_url":"https://github.com/jiuyi155/agxprobe","description":"CVE-2026-64747 AGXG14P count-bitmask OOB trigger probe (A15/iOS 26.5.2)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 20:50:48","updated_at":"2026-08-10 21:36:10","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 21:33:42","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:10","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329733115","cve_id":"CVE-2011-2523","name":"cve-2011-2523-vsftpd-validation-lab","owner":"alexojocyber","full_name":"alexojocyber/cve-2011-2523-vsftpd-validation-lab","html_url":"https://github.com/alexojocyber/cve-2011-2523-vsftpd-validation-lab","description":"Authorized Kali–Metasploitable2 lab using Python and Nmap NSE to validate CVE-2011-2523 in vsFTPd 2.3.4.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"vsftpd 2.3.4 downloaded between 20110630 and 20110703 contains a backdoor which opens a shell on port 6200/tcp.","created_at":"2026-08-10 20:09:47","updated_at":"2026-08-10 20:57:29","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 20:57:20","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:05","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1329629705","cve_id":"CVE-2026-23744","name":"CVE-2026-23744-PoC","owner":"amao26","full_name":"amao26/CVE-2026-23744-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/amao26/CVE-2026-23744-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-23744 is an unauthenticated command injection in MCPJam Inspector ≤1.4.2 via /api/mcp/connect. This POC exploits it by sending a crafted JSON payload to execute arbitrary commands, granting a reverse shell with PTY.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"MCPJam inspector is the local-first development platform for MCP servers. Versions 1.4.2 and earlier are vulnerable to remote code execution (RCE) vulnerability, which allows an attacker to send a crafted HTTP request that triggers the installation of an MCP server, leading to RCE. Since MCPJam inspector by default listens on 0.0.0.0 instead of 127.0.0.1, an attacker can trigger the RCE remotely via a simple HTTP request. Version 1.4.3 contains a patch.","created_at":"2026-08-10 18:07:16","updated_at":"2026-08-10 18:53:23","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 18:52:16","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329624505","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"GhostLock-GOT-W29","owner":"zzzxxxxxxxxxx","full_name":"zzzxxxxxxxxxx/GhostLock-GOT-W29","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzxxxxxxxxxx/GhostLock-GOT-W29","description":"CVE-2026-43499 (GhostLock) research on HUAWEI MatePad Pro 11 GOT-W29","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-10 18:01:08","updated_at":"2026-08-10 19:54:59","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 19:54:55","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:10","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329603900","cve_id":"CVE-2026-19264","name":"CVE-2026-19264","owner":"DarkLycn1976","full_name":"DarkLycn1976/CVE-2026-19264","html_url":"https://github.com/DarkLycn1976/CVE-2026-19264","description":"CVE-2026-19264 - Critical unauthenticated path traversal to full instance takeover in Postiz (< 2.22.1). Technical writeup: decode-order bypass, JWT_SECRET escalation, and analysis of the upstream fix.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 17:37:25","updated_at":"2026-08-10 17:53:29","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 17:53:03","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329601931","cve_id":"CVE-2023-31014","name":"CVE-2023-31014_Lab","owner":"LazyBear8372","full_name":"LazyBear8372/CVE-2023-31014_Lab","html_url":"https://github.com/LazyBear8372/CVE-2023-31014_Lab","description":"Educational Android lab for CVE-2023-31014 implicit intent hijacking","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"NVIDIA GeForce Now for Android contains a vulnerability in the game launcher component, where a malicious application on the same device can process the implicit intent meant for the streamer component. A successful exploit of this vulnerability may lead to limited information disclosure, denial of service, and code execution.","created_at":"2026-08-10 17:35:06","updated_at":"2026-08-10 17:35:48","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 17:35:10","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:07","cvss_score":4.2,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329519744","cve_id":"CVE-2025-59528","name":"CVE-2025-59528-PoC","owner":"sonnelon","full_name":"sonnelon/CVE-2025-59528-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/sonnelon/CVE-2025-59528-PoC","description":"The poc of CVE-2025-59528","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Flowise is a drag & drop user interface to build a customized large language model flow. In version 3.0.5, Flowise is vulnerable to remote code execution. The CustomMCP node allows users to input configuration settings for connecting to an external MCP server. This node parses the user-provided mcpServerConfig string to build the MCP server configuration. However, during this process, it executes JavaScript code without any security validation. Specifically, inside the convertToValidJSONString function, user input is directly passed to the Function() constructor, which evaluates and executes the input as JavaScript code. Since this runs with full Node.js runtime privileges, it can access dangerous modules such as child_process and fs. This issue has been patched in version 3.0.6.","created_at":"2026-08-10 15:54:32","updated_at":"2026-08-10 16:22:57","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 16:22:34","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 22:37:09","cvss_score":10,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329516757","cve_id":"CVE-2026-41710","name":"spring-retry-toolkit","owner":"NicheToolkit","full_name":"NicheToolkit/spring-retry-toolkit","html_url":"https://github.com/NicheToolkit/spring-retry-toolkit","description":"spring retry 1.3.x fix with niche tookkit for CVE-2026-41710","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An attacker can craft a large number of unique requests that trigger a failure, exhausting the capacity of the application-wide stateful retry cache. Once the cache is full, it permanently rejects any further updates, causing all later stateful retries and circuit breakers in the application to fail.\n\nAffected versions:\nSpring Retry 2.0.0 through 2.0.12; 1.3.0 through 1.3.4.","created_at":"2026-08-10 15:50:43","updated_at":"2026-08-10 15:50:47","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 15:50:44","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:09","cvss_score":5.9,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329513130","cve_id":"CVE-2026-20685","name":"CVE-2026-20685","owner":"HORKimhab","full_name":"HORKimhab/CVE-2026-20685","html_url":"https://github.com/HORKimhab/CVE-2026-20685","description":"CVE-2026-20685 - Draft or TODO","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An attacker in a privileged network position may be able to leak sensitive information. A path handling issue was addressed with improved validation. This issue is fixed in PCC Release 5E290.3.","created_at":"2026-08-10 15:46:13","updated_at":"2026-08-10 15:52:39","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 15:52:35","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:08","cvss_score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329448330","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64564","name":"sctphantom","owner":"suominen","full_name":"suominen/sctphantom","html_url":"https://github.com/suominen/sctphantom","description":"Tracking SCTPhantom (CVE-2026-64564), the Linux kernel SCTP ASCONF transport use-after-free","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 14:16:43","updated_at":"2026-08-10 15:48:34","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 15:48:08","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329442485","cve_id":"CVE-2020-23349","name":"CVE-2020-23349_Lab","owner":"LazyBear8372","full_name":"LazyBear8372/CVE-2020-23349_Lab","html_url":"https://github.com/LazyBear8372/CVE-2020-23349_Lab","description":"Educational Android lab for CVE-2020-23349 in Sina Weibo SDK 4.2.7","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An intent redirection issue was doscovered in Sina Weibo Android SDK 4.2.7 (com.sina.weibo.sdk.share.WbShareTransActivity), any unexported Activities could be started by the com.sina.weibo.sdk.share.WbShareTransActivity.","created_at":"2026-08-10 14:07:36","updated_at":"2026-08-10 14:09:04","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 14:07:42","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:05","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1329412958","cve_id":"CVE-2024-3094","name":"cs50-cybersecurity-final-project","owner":"namegabevictoire01-sys","full_name":"namegabevictoire01-sys/cs50-cybersecurity-final-project","html_url":"https://github.com/namegabevictoire01-sys/cs50-cybersecurity-final-project","description":"CS50 Cybersecurity Final Project - Analysis of CVE-2024-3094","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Malicious code was discovered in the upstream tarballs of xz, starting with version 5.6.0. The tarballs included extra .m4 files, which contained instructions for building with automake that did not exist in the repository. These instructions, through a series of complex obfuscations, extract a prebuilt object file from one of the test archives, which is then used to modify specific functions in the code while building the liblzma package. This issue results in liblzma being used by additional software, like sshd, to provide functionality that will be interpreted by the modified functions.","created_at":"2026-08-10 13:18:04","updated_at":"2026-08-10 13:24:10","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 13:24:04","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:07","cvss_score":10,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329354587","cve_id":"CVE-2024-29943","name":"CVE-2024-29943-but-with-wasm","owner":"SneakyNachos","full_name":"SneakyNachos/CVE-2024-29943-but-with-wasm","html_url":"https://github.com/SneakyNachos/CVE-2024-29943-but-with-wasm","description":"CVE-2024-29943, but with wasm","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"An attacker was able to perform an out-of-bounds read or write on a JavaScript object by fooling range-based bounds check elimination. This vulnerability affects Firefox < 124.0.1.","created_at":"2026-08-10 11:34:36","updated_at":"2026-08-10 11:59:44","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 11:59:32","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:07","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329341692","cve_id":"CVE-2022-38599","name":"CVE-2022-38599","owner":"arleyna","full_name":"arleyna/CVE-2022-38599","html_url":"https://github.com/arleyna/CVE-2022-38599","description":"Teleport v3.2.2, Teleport v3.5.6-rc6, and Teleport v3.6.3-b2 was discovered to contain an information leak via the /user/get-role-list web interface.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Teleport v3.2.2, Teleport v3.5.6-rc6, and Teleport v3.6.3-b2 was discovered to contain an information leak via the /user/get-role-list web interface.","created_at":"2026-08-10 11:11:23","updated_at":"2026-08-10 11:23:25","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 11:23:14","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:06","cvss_score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM"},{"id":"1329339990","cve_id":"CVE-2026-39987","name":"CVE-2026-39987-Poc","owner":"MADA0L","full_name":"MADA0L/CVE-2026-39987-Poc","html_url":"https://github.com/MADA0L/CVE-2026-39987-Poc","description":"Proof of Concept (PoC) WebSocket client for CVE-2026-39987 (Marimo Pre-Auth RCE), intended for authorized security testing.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"marimo is a reactive Python notebook. Prior to 0.23.0, Marimo has a Pre-Auth RCE vulnerability. The terminal WebSocket endpoint /terminal/ws lacks authentication validation, allowing an unauthenticated attacker to obtain a full PTY shell and execute arbitrary system commands. Unlike other WebSocket endpoints (e.g., /ws) that correctly call validate_auth() for authentication, the /terminal/ws endpoint only checks the running mode and platform support before accepting connections, completely skipping authentication verification. This vulnerability is fixed in 0.23.0.","created_at":"2026-08-10 11:08:03","updated_at":"2026-08-10 12:52:39","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 12:52:23","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.3,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329307009","cve_id":"CVE-2026-53787","name":"amasty-chekout-POC-rce","owner":"ChrisSEC2014","full_name":"ChrisSEC2014/amasty-chekout-POC-rce","html_url":"https://github.com/ChrisSEC2014/amasty-chekout-POC-rce","description":"my poc for CVE-2026-53787 ","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Amasty Order Attributes for Magento 2 before version 4.0.0 contains an unauthenticated arbitrary file upload vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to write arbitrary files to the store's media directory by submitting files of any type or name to the upload endpoint without authentication, session validation, or cart context. Attackers can upload PHP files to achieve remote code execution on servers where the media directory permits PHP execution, or alternatively enable malware hosting, stored cross-site scripting via HTML or SVG uploads, and path traversal to write files outside the intended upload directory.","created_at":"2026-08-10 10:00:28","updated_at":"2026-08-10 12:06:55","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 12:06:40","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 16:37:09","cvss_score":9.3,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329223466","cve_id":"CVE-2025-7026","name":"GIGABYTE-H510M-K-V2-BIOS-SMM-Reverse-Engineering-CVE-2025-7026-7027-7028-7029-Research","owner":"Tobss8","full_name":"Tobss8/GIGABYTE-H510M-K-V2-BIOS-SMM-Reverse-Engineering-CVE-2025-7026-7027-7028-7029-Research","html_url":"https://github.com/Tobss8/GIGABYTE-H510M-K-V2-BIOS-SMM-Reverse-Engineering-CVE-2025-7026-7027-7028-7029-Research","description":"Static reverse-engineering of a GIGABYTE H510M K V2 (`H510MKV2.F3`) BIOS image: full UEFI firmware-volume extraction analysis of the PI-spec SMM Core memory allocator and a targeted hunt for the four SMM memory-corruption vulnerabilities GIGABYTE/Binarly disclosed in 2025 (CVE-2025-7026 CVE-2025-7027 CVE-2025-7028 CVE-2025-7029).","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"A vulnerability in the Software SMI handler (SwSmiInputValue 0xB2) allows a local attacker to control the RBX register, which is used as an unchecked pointer in the CommandRcx0 function. If the contents at RBX match certain expected values (e.g., '$DB$' or '2DB$'), the function performs arbitrary writes to System Management RAM (SMRAM), leading to potential privilege escalation to System Management Mode (SMM) and persistent firmware compromise.","created_at":"2026-08-10 07:00:09","updated_at":"2026-08-10 07:10:45","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 07:10:34","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:08","cvss_score":8.2,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329211922","cve_id":"CVE-2025-3248","name":"langflow-exploit","owner":"preemware","full_name":"preemware/langflow-exploit","html_url":"https://github.com/preemware/langflow-exploit","description":"PoC for CVE-2025-3248: unauthenticated RCE in Langflow < 1.3.0 via /api/v1/validate/code.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Langflow versions prior to 1.3.0 are susceptible to code injection in \nthe /api/v1/validate/code endpoint. A remote and unauthenticated attacker can send crafted HTTP requests to execute arbitrary\ncode.","created_at":"2026-08-10 06:39:50","updated_at":"2026-08-10 07:09:36","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 06:39:53","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:08","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329190283","cve_id":"CVE-2026-17106","name":"CopyEscape-CVE-2026-17106","owner":"masasron","full_name":"masasron/CopyEscape-CVE-2026-17106","html_url":"https://github.com/masasron/CopyEscape-CVE-2026-17106","description":"PoC repository for the blog post CopyEscape: Taking Over Docker Hosts with docker cp","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 06:02:40","updated_at":"2026-08-11 13:41:18","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 06:04:41","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 16:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1329164149","cve_id":"CVE-2026-26119","name":"CVE-2026-26119","owner":"r3vpwnx","full_name":"r3vpwnx/CVE-2026-26119","html_url":"https://github.com/r3vpwnx/CVE-2026-26119","description":"WAC RCE - CVE-2026-26119 Windows Admin Center authenticated RCE via WinREST/PowerShell invokeCommand.","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"Improper authentication in Windows Admin Center allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges over a network.","created_at":"2026-08-10 05:21:00","updated_at":"2026-08-10 09:00:55","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 05:21:39","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:08","cvss_score":8.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329152473","cve_id":"CVE-2026-69084","name":"CVE-2026-69084-PoC","owner":"Boreas37","full_name":"Boreas37/CVE-2026-69084-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/Boreas37/CVE-2026-69084-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-69084/69085 — SiYuan arbitrary SQL execution via searchEmbedBlock + searchDocs SQLi (CVSS 9.9). Verified on v3.7.2, rejected on v3.7.3.","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 05:02:45","updated_at":"2026-08-10 05:05:49","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 05:02:49","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:09","cvss_score":9.9,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329144882","cve_id":"CVE-2026-26119","name":"CVE-2026-26119","owner":"Cyb3rWitch3r","full_name":"Cyb3rWitch3r/CVE-2026-26119","html_url":"https://github.com/Cyb3rWitch3r/CVE-2026-26119","description":"WAC RCE - CVE-2026-26119 Windows Admin Center authenticated RCE via WinREST/PowerShell invokeCommand.","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":"Improper authentication in Windows Admin Center allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges over a network.","created_at":"2026-08-10 04:50:49","updated_at":"2026-08-10 09:11:13","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 04:40:47","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:08","cvss_score":8.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329128067","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"Root-My-Galaxy-tests","owner":"OhLookItsTheIRS","full_name":"OhLookItsTheIRS/Root-My-Galaxy-tests","html_url":"https://github.com/OhLookItsTheIRS/Root-My-Galaxy-tests","description":"KSU installer for supported Samsung Galaxy firmware with CVE-2026-43499 (Note: Fork)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-10 04:27:51","updated_at":"2026-08-10 05:27:18","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 04:33:17","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 10:37:09","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1329075074","cve_id":"CVE-2025-59528","name":"CVE-2025-59528-PoC","owner":"Loaxert","full_name":"Loaxert/CVE-2025-59528-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/Loaxert/CVE-2025-59528-PoC","description":"PoC for CVE-2025-59528 used to achieve remote code execution on the Silentium machine at HTB","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Flowise is a drag & drop user interface to build a customized large language model flow. In version 3.0.5, Flowise is vulnerable to remote code execution. The CustomMCP node allows users to input configuration settings for connecting to an external MCP server. This node parses the user-provided mcpServerConfig string to build the MCP server configuration. However, during this process, it executes JavaScript code without any security validation. Specifically, inside the convertToValidJSONString function, user input is directly passed to the Function() constructor, which evaluates and executes the input as JavaScript code. Since this runs with full Node.js runtime privileges, it can access dangerous modules such as child_process and fs. This issue has been patched in version 3.0.6.","created_at":"2026-08-10 03:13:57","updated_at":"2026-08-10 03:20:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 03:20:17","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 04:37:07","cvss_score":10,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1329013712","cve_id":"CVE-2026-34910","name":"CVE-2026-34910-PoC","owner":"Boreas37","full_name":"Boreas37/CVE-2026-34910-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/Boreas37/CVE-2026-34910-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-34910/34909 — UniFi OS unauth RCE + file read via ..%2f auth bypass (CVSS 10.0, KEV, Mirai ITW)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"A malicious actor with access to the network could exploit an Improper Input Validation vulnerability found in UniFi OS devices to execute a Command Injection.","created_at":"2026-08-10 01:58:00","updated_at":"2026-08-10 02:57:49","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 02:57:44","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 04:37:08","cvss_score":10,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1328930950","cve_id":"CVE-2026-15038","name":"By-Poloss..-..CVE-2026-15038-POC","owner":"Polosss","full_name":"Polosss/By-Poloss..-..CVE-2026-15038-POC","html_url":"https://github.com/Polosss/By-Poloss..-..CVE-2026-15038-POC","description":" POC 4 CVE-2026-15038","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-10 00:19:47","updated_at":"2026-08-10 00:24:30","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 00:24:25","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 04:37:08","cvss_score":9.8,"severity":"CRITICAL"},{"id":"1328905026","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"xss2shell","owner":"0xlipon","full_name":"0xlipon/xss2shell","html_url":"https://github.com/0xlipon/xss2shell","description":"🔥 XSS2Shell — CVE-2026-64638 Scanner & PoC Toolkit","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 23:50:57","updated_at":"2026-08-10 00:20:27","pushed_at":"2026-08-10 00:20:11","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 04:37:08","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1328817336","cve_id":"CVE-2026-4282","name":"CVE-2026-4282-Scanner","owner":"hexissam","full_name":"hexissam/CVE-2026-4282-Scanner","html_url":"https://github.com/hexissam/CVE-2026-4282-Scanner","description":"Non-intrusive version-based vulnerability scanner for CVE-2026-4282 (Keycloak SingleUseObjectProvider isolation flaw enabling authorization code forgery & privilege escalation)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"A flaw was found in Keycloak. The SingleUseObjectProvider, a global key-value store, lacks proper type and namespace isolation. This vulnerability allows an unauthenticated attacker to forge authorization codes. Successful exploitation can lead to the creation of admin-capable access tokens, resulting in privilege escalation.","created_at":"2026-08-09 22:13:13","updated_at":"2026-08-09 22:16:29","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 22:14:12","inserted_at":"2026-08-10 04:37:08","cvss_score":7.4,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1328729935","cve_id":"CVE-2026-41091","name":"RedSun-","owner":"s4m98","full_name":"s4m98/RedSun-","html_url":"https://github.com/s4m98/RedSun-","description":"Windwos Zero Day Local PrivESc Exploit (CVE-2026-41091)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Improper link resolution before file access ('link following') in Microsoft Defender allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges locally.","created_at":"2026-08-09 20:23:46","updated_at":"2026-08-09 20:27:48","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 20:24:59","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 22:37:08","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1328704024","cve_id":"CVE-2017-8464","name":"POC-CVE-2017-8464-OpenCalculator","owner":"PlayBoiSK8","full_name":"PlayBoiSK8/POC-CVE-2017-8464-OpenCalculator","html_url":"https://github.com/PlayBoiSK8/POC-CVE-2017-8464-OpenCalculator","description":"Exploiting the .lnk vulnerability and operating system handling mechanisms regarding explorer.exe and USB drives.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Windows Shell in Microsoft Windows Server 2008 SP2 and R2 SP1, Windows 7 SP1, Windows 8, Windows 8.1, Windows Server 2012 Gold and R2, Windows RT 8.1, Windows 10 Gold, 1511, 1607, 1703, and Windows Server 2016 allows local users or remote attackers to execute arbitrary code via a crafted .LNK file, which is not properly handled during icon display in Windows Explorer or any other application that parses the icon of the shortcut. aka \"LNK Remote Code Execution Vulnerability.\"","created_at":"2026-08-09 19:49:41","updated_at":"2026-08-09 19:56:09","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 19:56:00","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 22:37:04","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328590726","cve_id":"CVE-2026-63030","name":"WP2Shell","owner":"g0d150ne","full_name":"g0d150ne/WP2Shell","html_url":"https://github.com/g0d150ne/WP2Shell","description":"WP2Shell is a powerful and modular exploit framework that combines two critical WordPress vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-63030 and CVE-2026-60137) to achieve complete compromise of a target site without any credentials. ","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 17:26:51","updated_at":"2026-08-11 06:08:17","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 05:54:00","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328541859","cve_id":"CVE-2026-9645","name":"CVE-2026-9645-ScadaBR-Analysis","owner":"0xmhany","full_name":"0xmhany/CVE-2026-9645-ScadaBR-Analysis","html_url":"https://github.com/0xmhany/CVE-2026-9645-ScadaBR-Analysis","description":"Technical vulnerability analysis and CVE briefing for CVE-2026-9645 affecting ScadaBR.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Exposed methods allow authenticated users to create and execute arbitrary JavaScript code on the server. The scripts execute with full access, enabling complete system compromise as commands are executed as root.","created_at":"2026-08-09 16:18:11","updated_at":"2026-08-09 16:29:32","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 16:29:07","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 22:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328532394","cve_id":"CVE-2021-44228","name":"log4j-shell-poc","owner":"Jiahong-Guan","full_name":"Jiahong-Guan/log4j-shell-poc","html_url":"https://github.com/Jiahong-Guan/log4j-shell-poc","description":"A Proof-Of-Concept for the CVE-2021-44228 vulnerability.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Apache Log4j2 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (excluding security releases 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1) JNDI features used in configuration, log messages, and parameters do not protect against attacker controlled LDAP and other JNDI related endpoints. An attacker who can control log messages or log message parameters can execute arbitrary code loaded from LDAP servers when message lookup substitution is enabled. From log4j 2.15.0, this behavior has been disabled by default. From version 2.16.0 (along with 2.12.2, 2.12.3, and 2.3.1), this functionality has been completely removed. Note that this vulnerability is specific to log4j-core and does not affect log4net, log4cxx, or other Apache Logging Services projects.","created_at":"2026-08-09 16:04:50","updated_at":"2026-08-09 20:54:37","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 20:54:21","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 22:37:05","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328532335","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"XSS2Shell","owner":"g0d150ne","full_name":"g0d150ne/XSS2Shell","html_url":"https://github.com/g0d150ne/XSS2Shell","description":"XSS2Shell ULTIMATE v3.0 is a powerful exploitation tool that chains Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities in WordPress to achieve Remote Code Execution (RCE). This tool exploits CVE-2026-64638 to gain full control over vulnerable WordPress installations.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 16:04:45","updated_at":"2026-08-11 06:08:48","pushed_at":"2026-08-11 05:55:50","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1328393493","cve_id":"CVE-2026-19195","name":"CVE-2026-19195-PoC","owner":"patrickt2017","full_name":"patrickt2017/CVE-2026-19195-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/patrickt2017/CVE-2026-19195-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-19195 Proof of Concept","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 12:31:39","updated_at":"2026-08-09 12:40:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 12:40:20","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 16:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328379364","cve_id":"CVE-2026-19193","name":"CVE-2026-19193-PoC","owner":"patrickt2017","full_name":"patrickt2017/CVE-2026-19193-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/patrickt2017/CVE-2026-19193-PoC","description":"CVE-2026-19193 Proof of Concept","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 12:09:24","updated_at":"2026-08-09 12:13:34","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 12:11:56","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 16:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1328360976","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"Root-My-Galaxy","owner":"ruik-tech","full_name":"ruik-tech/Root-My-Galaxy","html_url":"https://github.com/ruik-tech/Root-My-Galaxy","description":"KSU installer for supported Samsung Galaxy firmware with CVE-2026-43499","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-09 11:39:07","updated_at":"2026-08-09 20:08:34","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 11:42:45","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 22:37:08","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1328280706","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","owner":"jendmaoul","full_name":"jendmaoul/XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/jendmaoul/XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","description":"CVE-2026-64638 — WordPress Pre-Auth Reflected XSS → RCE via DOM Clobbering + Application Password Theft + REST API Plugin Activation. Dual-mode PoC (XSS chain & direct).","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 09:17:29","updated_at":"2026-08-09 09:35:56","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 17:12:07","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 10:37:08","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327994300","cve_id":"CVE-2026-63030","name":"wp2shell-Exploit-Waf-Bypass","owner":"M4xSec","full_name":"M4xSec/wp2shell-Exploit-Waf-Bypass","html_url":"https://github.com/M4xSec/wp2shell-Exploit-Waf-Bypass","description":"WordPress Pre-Auth RCE Exploit + Scanner + WAF Bypass | CVE-2026-63030 + CVE-2026-60137 | Go + Python + Metasploit modules + Docker lab","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 02:22:08","updated_at":"2026-08-09 02:41:07","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 02:39:56","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 04:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327954467","cve_id":"CVE-2026-27912","name":"ResetNightmare-impacket","owner":"mihat2","full_name":"mihat2/ResetNightmare-impacket","html_url":"https://github.com/mihat2/ResetNightmare-impacket","description":"CVE-2026-27912 (ResetNightmare) — Linux/impacket port of Semperis Community's Invoke-ResetNightmare PoC","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Improper authorization in Windows Kerberos allows an authorized attacker to elevate privileges over an adjacent network.","created_at":"2026-08-09 01:36:35","updated_at":"2026-08-09 01:40:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 01:40:34","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 04:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327912334","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64561","name":"CVE-2026-64561-Kernel-Fix","owner":"chuzhongyun","full_name":"chuzhongyun/CVE-2026-64561-Kernel-Fix","html_url":"https://github.com/chuzhongyun/CVE-2026-64561-Kernel-Fix","description":"Linux 内核升级指南 - 修复 CVE-2026-64561","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 00:49:30","updated_at":"2026-08-11 06:54:10","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 00:50:24","inserted_at":"2026-08-11 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327885254","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64600","name":"CVE-2026-64600-RefluXFS","owner":"masrikky","full_name":"masrikky/CVE-2026-64600-RefluXFS","html_url":"https://github.com/masrikky/CVE-2026-64600-RefluXFS","description":"A Linux kernel local privilege escalation affecting the XFS filesystem copy-on-write (CoW) path.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09 00:18:19","updated_at":"2026-08-09 00:26:00","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 00:25:55","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 04:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327759976","cve_id":"CVE-2026-60004","name":"CVE-2026-60004-poc-gitea","owner":"gagaltotal","full_name":"gagaltotal/CVE-2026-60004-poc-gitea","html_url":"https://github.com/gagaltotal/CVE-2026-60004-poc-gitea","description":"CVE-2026-60004 — Gitea Pre-Auth RCE via diffpatch hook injection","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 22:08:31","updated_at":"2026-08-09 01:41:47","pushed_at":"2026-08-09 01:41:43","inserted_at":"2026-08-09 04:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327693668","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638-PoC-Exploit","owner":"tc4dy","full_name":"tc4dy/CVE-2026-64638-PoC-Exploit","html_url":"https://github.com/tc4dy/CVE-2026-64638-PoC-Exploit","description":"🛡️ CVE-2026-64638 - WordPress Security Assessment Suite (CVSS 8.9) | WordPress 4.7.0-7.0.2 pentest toolkit. Includes vulnerability assessment & advanced analysis modules. 🐍 Safe Check & Exploit, 2 mode. Advanced Blue&Red Team Best 2026-64638 Toolkit, Authorized use only. Stay Legal <3zd","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 20:53:39","updated_at":"2026-08-08 20:56:07","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 20:57:26","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327685508","cve_id":"CVE-2026-3844","name":"CVE-2026-3844","owner":"AnggaTechI","full_name":"AnggaTechI/CVE-2026-3844","html_url":"https://github.com/AnggaTechI/CVE-2026-3844","description":"CVE-2026-3844 — Unauthenticated Arbitrary File Upload to RCE in Breeze Cache (WordPress).  CVSS 9.8 CRITICAL. Mass scanner + auto shell injector with multi-threading.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"The Breeze Cache plugin for WordPress is vulnerable to arbitrary file uploads due to missing file type validation in the 'fetch_gravatar_from_remote' function in all versions up to, and including, 2.4.4. This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to upload arbitrary files on the affected site's server which may make remote code execution possible. The vulnerability can only be exploited if \"Host Files Locally - Gravatars\" is enabled, which is disabled by default.","created_at":"2026-08-08 20:43:54","updated_at":"2026-08-08 21:05:40","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 21:05:37","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327683943","cve_id":"CVE-2026-43499","name":"GhostLock-Galaxy","owner":"wxxsfxyzm","full_name":"wxxsfxyzm/GhostLock-Galaxy","html_url":"https://github.com/wxxsfxyzm/GhostLock-Galaxy","description":"Root your Galaxy using CVE-2026-43499","stargazers_count":"4","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtmutex: Use waiter::task instead of current in remove_waiter()\n\nremove_waiter() is used by the slowlock paths, but it is also used for\nproxy-lock rollback in rt_mutex_start_proxy_lock() when invoked from\nfutex_requeue().\n\nIn the latter case waiter::task is not current, but remove_waiter()\noperates on current for the dequeue operation. That results in several\nproblems:\n\n  1) the rbtree dequeue happens without waiter::task::pi_lock being held\n\n  2) the waiter task's pi_blocked_on state is not cleared, which leaves a\n     dangling pointer primed for UAF around.\n\n  3) rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain() operates on the wrong top priority waiter\n     task\n\nUse waiter::task instead of current in all related operations in\nremove_waiter() to cure those problems.\n\n[ tglx: Fixup rt_mutex_adjust_prio_chain(), add a comment and amend the\n  \tchangelog ]","created_at":"2026-08-08 20:41:33","updated_at":"2026-08-08 21:29:53","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 21:09:57","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327588935","cve_id":"CVE-2023-32233","name":"CVE-2023-32233-reproduction","owner":"BurnSkyup","full_name":"BurnSkyup/CVE-2023-32233-reproduction","html_url":"https://github.com/BurnSkyup/CVE-2023-32233-reproduction","description":"A Linux-related vulnerability","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In the Linux kernel through 6.3.1, a use-after-free in Netfilter nf_tables when processing batch requests can be abused to perform arbitrary read and write operations on kernel memory. Unprivileged local users can obtain root privileges. This occurs because anonymous sets are mishandled.","created_at":"2026-08-08 18:11:50","updated_at":"2026-08-08 20:29:22","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 19:29:18","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:05","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327573893","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638","owner":"HackSpeak","full_name":"HackSpeak/CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/HackSpeak/CVE-2026-64638","description":"XSS2Shell (CVE-2026-64638) WordPress pre-auth XSS to RCE PoC mirror — WordSec, MIT; for authorized security testing","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 17:51:12","updated_at":"2026-08-08 18:07:41","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 18:07:24","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327571084","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638","owner":"4minx","full_name":"4minx/CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/4minx/CVE-2026-64638","description":"CVE-2026-64638 (XSS2shell) POC.","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 17:48:02","updated_at":"2026-08-08 21:02:45","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 17:58:46","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327482532","cve_id":"CVE-2026-63077","name":"CVE-2026-63077","owner":"AnggaTechI","full_name":"AnggaTechI/CVE-2026-63077","html_url":"https://github.com/AnggaTechI/CVE-2026-63077","description":"CVE-2026-63077 — Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in JetBrains TeamCity via agent polling protocol deserialization. CVSS 9.8 CRITICAL. Mass exploitation tool with interactive shell, multi-threading, and real-time result logging.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 15:32:09","updated_at":"2026-08-08 15:47:46","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 15:47:43","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327386258","cve_id":"CVE-2026-18953","name":"CVE-2026-18953","owner":"ronamosa","full_name":"ronamosa/CVE-2026-18953","html_url":"https://github.com/ronamosa/CVE-2026-18953","description":"PoC for CVE-2026-18953 — arbitrary file write (CWE-22) in awslabs.aws-transform-mcp-server's get_resource tool via the savePath parameter","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 12:41:26","updated_at":"2026-08-08 12:45:53","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 12:45:49","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:07","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327339276","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64561","name":"CVE-2026-64561","owner":"HackSpeak","full_name":"HackSpeak/CVE-2026-64561","html_url":"https://github.com/HackSpeak/CVE-2026-64561","description":"Zapscape (CVE-2026-64561) KVM/x86 shadow MMU UAF guest-to-host escape PoC mirror — V4bel/@v4bel, MIT; for authorized security testing","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 11:13:23","updated_at":"2026-08-08 11:20:14","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 11:20:11","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327337309","cve_id":"CVE-2019-14287","name":"Sudo-Agent-CTF-","owner":"NyxRecon","full_name":"NyxRecon/Sudo-Agent-CTF-","html_url":"https://github.com/NyxRecon/Sudo-Agent-CTF-","description":"Write-up do Sudo Agent CTF (TryHackMe), com enumeração, exploração web, esteganografia, SSH e privilege escalation via CVE-2019-14287.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"In Sudo before 1.8.28, an attacker with access to a Runas ALL sudoer account can bypass certain policy blacklists and session PAM modules, and can cause incorrect logging, by invoking sudo with a crafted user ID. For example, this allows bypass of !root configuration, and USER= logging, for a \"sudo -u \\#$((0xffffffff))\" command.","created_at":"2026-08-08 11:09:27","updated_at":"2026-08-08 11:40:35","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 11:40:30","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:04","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327310403","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638-POC","owner":"imbas007","full_name":"imbas007/CVE-2026-64638-POC","html_url":"https://github.com/imbas007/CVE-2026-64638-POC","description":"CVE-2026-64638: WordPress Pre-auth XSS → RCE (XSS2Shell) PoC","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 10:20:11","updated_at":"2026-08-08 10:24:52","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 10:24:48","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:08","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327302379","cve_id":"CVE-2017-9757","name":"IPFire_2.19_RCE_Authenticated","owner":"joaoaugustom","full_name":"joaoaugustom/IPFire_2.19_RCE_Authenticated","html_url":"https://github.com/joaoaugustom/IPFire_2.19_RCE_Authenticated","description":"This exploit is based on CVE-2017-9757 and was built upon the original exploit by 0x09AL.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"IPFire 2.19 has a Remote Command Injection vulnerability in ids.cgi via the OINKCODE parameter, which is mishandled by a shell. This can be exploited directly by authenticated users, or through CSRF.","created_at":"2026-08-08 10:05:36","updated_at":"2026-08-08 10:14:22","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 10:12:42","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 16:37:03","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327272773","cve_id":"CVE-2026-63077","name":"teamcity-CVE-2026-63077-pcap","owner":"BoredHackerBlog","full_name":"BoredHackerBlog/teamcity-CVE-2026-63077-pcap","html_url":"https://github.com/BoredHackerBlog/teamcity-CVE-2026-63077-pcap","description":"teamcity teamcity-CVE-2026-63077 exploitation pcap","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 09:10:31","updated_at":"2026-08-08 09:23:00","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 09:22:56","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327260789","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638-WordPress-Core-XSS2Shell","owner":"renzi25031469","full_name":"renzi25031469/CVE-2026-64638-WordPress-Core-XSS2Shell","html_url":"https://github.com/renzi25031469/CVE-2026-64638-WordPress-Core-XSS2Shell","description":"Template Nuclei para detecção não-intrusiva do XSS2Shell, um parser differential pré-autenticado no WordPress Core que permite injeção de elementos DOM na página de login, servindo de base para uma cadeia de XSS → RCE.","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 08:48:18","updated_at":"2026-08-08 08:51:38","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 08:50:40","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327223952","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638","owner":"0xBlackash","full_name":"0xBlackash/CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/0xBlackash/CVE-2026-64638","description":"CVE-2026-64638","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 07:44:35","updated_at":"2026-08-08 07:48:30","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 07:48:25","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327201129","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","owner":"Linuxhackingid-official","full_name":"Linuxhackingid-official/XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/Linuxhackingid-official/XSS2Shell-CVE-2026-64638","description":"CVE-2026-64638 — WordPress Pre-Auth Reflected XSS → RCE via DOM Clobbering + Application Password Theft + REST API Plugin Activation. Dual-mode PoC (XSS chain & direct).","stargazers_count":"2","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 07:07:13","updated_at":"2026-08-08 20:26:53","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 17:12:07","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327167144","cve_id":"CVE-2026-71554","name":"poc-h2-CVE-2026-71554","owner":"SunandM","full_name":"SunandM/poc-h2-CVE-2026-71554","html_url":"https://github.com/SunandM/poc-h2-CVE-2026-71554","description":"PoC for CVE-2026-71554 - h2 duplicate Host header request smuggling primitive (fixed in 4.4.1)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 06:15:48","updated_at":"2026-08-08 06:19:15","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 06:19:11","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327166541","cve_id":"CVE-2026-71554","name":"poc-h2-duplicate-host","owner":"SunandM","full_name":"SunandM/poc-h2-duplicate-host","html_url":"https://github.com/SunandM/poc-h2-duplicate-host","description":"PoC for CVE-2026-71554 — h2 duplicate Host header request smuggling primitive (fixed in 4.4.1)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 06:14:52","updated_at":"2026-08-08 06:14:53","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 06:14:53","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327162672","cve_id":"CVE-2026-57858","name":"CVE-2026-57858","owner":"zylideum","full_name":"zylideum/CVE-2026-57858","html_url":"https://github.com/zylideum/CVE-2026-57858","description":"Wormable exploit for CVE-2026-57858","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 06:09:14","updated_at":"2026-08-08 06:09:19","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 06:09:15","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327159643","cve_id":"CVE-2025-32432","name":"CVE-2025-32432-PoC","owner":"EzraMansor","full_name":"EzraMansor/CVE-2025-32432-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/EzraMansor/CVE-2025-32432-PoC","description":"A simple PoC on the Remote Code Execution (RCE) Vulnerability of CraftCMS designated as CVE-2025-32432 written in Go","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Craft is a flexible, user-friendly CMS for creating custom digital experiences on the web and beyond. Starting from version 3.0.0-RC1 to before 3.9.15, 4.0.0-RC1 to before 4.14.15, and 5.0.0-RC1 to before 5.6.17, Craft is vulnerable to remote code execution. This is a high-impact, low-complexity attack vector. This issue has been patched in versions 3.9.15, 4.14.15, and 5.6.17, and is an additional fix for CVE-2023-41892.","created_at":"2026-08-08 06:05:02","updated_at":"2026-08-08 06:21:30","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 06:21:27","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:08","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327112554","cve_id":"CVE-2026-55957","name":"CVE-2026-55957-PoC","owner":"mdvpat","full_name":"mdvpat/CVE-2026-55957-PoC","html_url":"https://github.com/mdvpat/CVE-2026-55957-PoC","description":"Reproducible Docker lab for the Apache Tomcat JNDIRealm GSSAPI authentication bypass","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"Missing Critical Step in Authentication vulnerability in Apache Tomcat when the JNDIRealm was configured to authenticate binds using GSSAPI allowed attackers to authenticate without provided the correct password.\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0-M1 through 11.0.4, from 10.1.0-M1 through 10.1.36, from 9.0.0.M1 through 9.0.100, from 8.5.0 through 8.5.100, from 7.0.0 through 7.0.109.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.5, 10.1.37 or 9.0.101, which fixes the issue.","created_at":"2026-08-08 05:02:00","updated_at":"2026-08-08 05:15:22","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 05:15:13","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327099432","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"CVE-2026-64638","owner":"5yu4n","full_name":"5yu4n/CVE-2026-64638","html_url":"https://github.com/5yu4n/CVE-2026-64638","description":"CVE-2026-64638","stargazers_count":"1","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 04:45:44","updated_at":"2026-08-08 04:58:48","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 04:58:45","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 10:37:09","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"},{"id":"1327068367","cve_id":"CVE-2026-49844","name":"log4j-check","owner":"xiaoqiMikko","full_name":"xiaoqiMikko/log4j-check","html_url":"https://github.com/xiaoqiMikko/log4j-check","description":"log4j 2025/2026 年 7 条「配置静默失效」CVE 自查:按 CVE×模块 判定 4 个模块,结构化解析 log4j2 配置做 applicability 降噪,并算出该升到哪个版本才一次到位(6 条写 2.25.4,但有一条要 2.25.5,而它 Dependabot 报不出来) CVE-2026-49844 / CVE-2026-34477","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 04:09:13","updated_at":"2026-08-08 15:54:24","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 04:10:15","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 22:37:07","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1327005225","cve_id":"CVE-2025-55182","name":"CVE-2025-55182-Advanced-React-Server-Components-RCE-Exploit","owner":"CerberusMrXi","full_name":"CerberusMrXi/CVE-2025-55182-Advanced-React-Server-Components-RCE-Exploit","html_url":"https://github.com/CerberusMrXi/CVE-2025-55182-Advanced-React-Server-Components-RCE-Exploit","description":"Advanced React Server Components RCE scanner for CVE-2025-55182. Features: multi-stage fingerprinting, vulnerability verification, DNS exfiltration, interactive shell, payload obfuscation, and professional reporting (JSON/HTML/PDF). Authorized testing only. ","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":"A pre-authentication remote code execution vulnerability exists in React Server Components versions 19.0.0, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, and 19.2.0 including the following packages: react-server-dom-parcel, react-server-dom-turbopack, and react-server-dom-webpack. The vulnerable code unsafely deserializes payloads from HTTP requests to Server Function endpoints.","created_at":"2026-08-08 02:57:25","updated_at":"2026-08-08 03:30:40","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 03:30:27","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 04:37:09","cvss_score":null,"severity":"UNKNOWN"},{"id":"1326997123","cve_id":"CVE-2026-64638","name":"XSS2Shell","owner":"wordsec","full_name":"wordsec/XSS2Shell","html_url":"https://github.com/wordsec/XSS2Shell","description":"Wordpress Pre-auth XSS to RCE exploit PoC (xss2shell & CVE-2026-64638)","stargazers_count":"0","vuln_description":null,"created_at":"2026-08-08 02:48:46","updated_at":"2026-08-08 03:32:18","pushed_at":"2026-08-08 03:12:28","inserted_at":"2026-08-08 04:37:09","cvss_score":8.9,"severity":"HIGH"}]}]}]
